.SH DESCRIPTION
A bare \fBjevcode\fR opens the interactive session TUI: a scrollback\-native
transcript, a composer, the Jev decision pane and a status line. \fBjevcode
run\fR runs one task and exits with the run\(aqs code. Every human decision
(approve, decline, steer, pause, abort) is a key or a slash command; keys
never appear in logs, secrets are detected at every entry point and the
sandbox confines every command the generator proposes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B chat
interactive session (the default when no command is given)
.TP
.B run
run one task; \-\-resume continues a stored run
.TP
.B config
print the resolved configuration with the source of every value
.TP
.B bench
run the benchmark suites
.TP
.B perf
run the performance gates
.TP
.B login
store an API key (masked prompt or \-\-*\-stdin)
.TP
.B logout
remove a stored API key
.TP
.B sessions
list, reindex, prune or unlock sessions
.TP
.B report
write a redacted support bundle for a run
.TP
.B why
explain one Jev decision of a stored run
.TP
.B calibration
reliability report over this workspace\(aqs runs
.TP
.B completion
print the shell completion script (bash|zsh|fish)
.TP
.B upgrade
upgrade through the detected package manager
